#lang treason

;; Slides: "The Fix", "The Hard Part: Inside a Bad Macro Use" and
;; "Spec-Driven Subexpression Expansion"
;;
;; The header of the my-define use is empty: no function name, no parameters.
;; The macro can't expand, but body:expr says each body form is an expression,
;; so treason expands the body on its own and you get services in it.
;;
;; You can see that from the errors: besides the bad use, treason reports sqrt,
;; sqr, x and y as unbound, which it can only know by expanding the body. (x
;; and y would be parameters if the header were there, and treason has no sqrt
;; or sqr.)

(define-syntax my-define
  (syntax-rules ()
    [(my-define (f x ...)
       body:expr ...)
     (define f
       (lambda (x ...)
         (block body ...)))]))

(my-define ()
  (sqrt (+ (sqr x) (sqr y))))
